<Layout title="About — Zahin Kabir" active="About"><section class="wrap page-top"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / ZAHIN KABIR</p><h1>Hi, I’m Zahin.</h1><p class="lede">Robotics &amp; mechanical engineer, but secretly a chemical engineer.</p></section><section class="wrap prose-grid"><h2>What I’ve been doing</h2><div><p>I’m studying Chemical Engineering at Purdue and expecting to graduate in 2027. I’m also minoring in Materials Science &amp; Engineering, Philosophy, and Japanese.</p><p>Ask me about work! I’m an R&amp;D Mechanical Engineer at Shinkei, where we’re building robots that support sustainable fish harvesting. Before that, I worked in R&amp;D/Quality Engineering at Keurig Dr Pepper and R&amp;D Process Engineering at Ourobio.</p><p>Ask me about my personal projects too. I’m developing a smart coffee roaster for home use, with computer vision, multimodal sensing, and machine learning. It’s still a work in progress; the project page has the build photos and current plan.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}experience/`}>See where I’ve worked ↗</a></div></section></Layout>
